    "done_when": "The worker prompt composed in reckon/crew/prompts.py states the small-node rule:\n- A node is small when its diff has at most 50 changed lines (added plus deleted), or when it changes no product source or tests and has at most 300 changed lines.\n- A small node writes one landing: line in its manifest, stating what changed and its measure's figure. It writes neither evidence prose nor a figure unless its done-when names that artifact, and naming one does not permit the other.\n- Any single data file above 300,000 bytes belongs in the run directory, not the repository.\nThe rule appears once, in the prompt's evidence contract beside the existing landing: sentence at prompts.py:73-75, and is not repeated elsewhere.\n\ntests/test_small_node_prompt.py composes the prompt for a small implement node with the existing builder, the way tests/test_crew_prompts.py does, and asserts each of the three rules by its own wording. It also asserts that a node whose done-when names a figure is told it may write the figure but not evidence prose. The existing prompt tests (tests/test_crew_prompts.py, tests/test_the_prompt_carries_the_evidence_contract.py, tests/test_skill_contract_parity.py) keep their base failing ids and add none.\n\nThe manifest writes baseline_suite and after_suite each as one line of armed JSON: revision, command with no placeholder, exit_status, completed, failure_count, failure_ids, log_path. The head arm runs at the committed head, and every gate log opens with one line naming its revision, tree and command. The declared negative control is applied and observed to fail, and its log's absolute path is in the manifest with an EXIT= line and the FAILED id. This node is itself small, so it writes one landing: line and no evidence prose or figure.",
    "estimated_hours": null,
    "goal": "State the small-node rule in the worker prompt, so a small node records one landing line, writes prose or a figure only when its done-when names that artifact, and keeps large data files in the run directory",
    "id": "small-node-prompt-rule",
